#     callers are byte-identical); add/remove single+batch mirrors; clone/init/
#     freeze covered (static bitmap blocks all rungs — conservative);
#     is_via_blocked_rung(gx, gy, rung).
#   router.rs: RouterOptions.via_rung (default 0 = baseline), consulted at the
#     via-transition test. New methods sit in existing #[pymethods] impls.
#   Cargo.toml: 0.19.3 -> 0.20.0 (rides the already-pending 0.20.0 release).
#
# Python integration REQUIRED before this does anything (not in this patch —
# the worktree's Python is frozen under a live A/B):
#   1. obstacle_cache: NetObstacleData.blocked_vias_small; builders compute the
#      via-block cell set a SECOND time at the small-rung reserve
#      (fab_floor_ladder advanced dia/2 + clearance + track/2) and
#      add/remove_net_obstacles_from_cache stamp/remove both maps.
#   2. run_obstacle_audit: extend get_stats consumers + hard-set labels with
#      blocked_vias_small (the leak audit must cover every rung map).
#   3. _via_rung_retry: replace the free-via overlay + sampling with
#      router.opts.via_rung = 1 for the retry (reset after), and register the
#      small (dia, drill) in pcb_data._unblock_via_sizes for each via cell of
#      the returned path so emission ships the small rung (#339 re-validates).
#   4. README.md version history: 0.20.0 — per-rung via legality (#568).
#   5. Remove the overlay's h2h site-validator (the rung map + stamps make it
#      redundant) once both maps are stamped from the same geometry.
#
